Z||000000||fierose||07-03-2000||10:21 PM||||Just checked my manual tranny fluid (was half a quart low).  Well I went to fill it up looked in the book (Hayes) and it said for an 85 manual to put in 5W-30 or dexron II.  My first question is what's the best fluid to use and also if the two are mixed will it hurt anyting.  What are the likely seals I should check to correct the leakage problem.  Where do you find a speedo sensor o-ring?  Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000001||webbee||07-03-2000||10:52 PM||||I don't think it makes any difference. They are both thin oils with lots of additives. Mixing isn't usually a problem. If it's red it's got Dextron in it already.  If it' s dirty then you should fix the leaks and then you decide what your going to use from then on. Don't know about seals. Try Autozone,or whoever you have in your area. The dealers the last choice d/t expense.||||reg||1
